  "worked_solution": "We can calculate the lateral surface area of a cylinder using the formula\n\n$$\n{S}_{L}=2\\pi rh,\n$$\n\nwhere $r$ is the radius and $h$ is the height of the cylinder.\n\nSubstituting $r=12\\,\\text{in}$ and $h=14\\,\\text{in}$ into the formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{L} & =2\\pi (12)(14)=336\\pi \\,{\\text{in}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
